Add `zustand` to `apps/patterns/package.json` (already an allowed dependency per the state-management rule).

### Pre-implementation probes (do these in commit 1)

Before building the full stack manager, two short empirical checks resolve the architectural assumptions:

1. *SSR slot survival under `client:only`.* Add `data-probe="ssr"` to the `<article>` in `[...slug].astro`. Add a 10-line `client:load` React component mounted inside Base that logs `document.querySelector('[data-probe="ssr"]')` after a microtask. If it logs `null`, AppShell's hydration wiped the slot — the JSON blob path is mandatory. If it logs the element, we have the option to skip the Container API and lift HTML from the live DOM instead (cheaper and simpler).
2. *Container API availability in Astro 6.3.* Confirm `experimental_AstroContainer` exists and renders MDX correctly. If not, fall back to the `<template>` element strategy noted earlier.

Both probes are throwaway and inform whether commit 2 (the real implementation) uses the JSON blob or the live-DOM path.

### Verification

1. `pnpm --filter @pattern-plgrnd/patterns dev` then open `http://localhost:4321/patterns/operations/undo`. Confirm the page renders identically to today (single pane, no horizontal scroll).
2. Click an internal pattern link inside the article. Expect: a second pane slides in to the right; URL gains `?stackedNotes=…`; the original article stays visible; focus moves to the new pane's heading.
3. Click a link inside the *second* pane. Expect: a third pane appears to its right; no fourth, no growth past the click source.
4. Click a link inside the *first* pane while two follow it. Expect: panes 2 and 3 are dropped and replaced with the new target as pane 2 (truncate-and-append).
5. Press browser back. Expect: stack pops one pane; URL updates accordingly.
6. Copy a deep stack URL, paste it in a fresh tab. Expect: all panes render in order; viewport is scrolled to the rightmost; focus is in the rightmost.
7. Click a sidebar link mid-exploration. Expect: full navigation; new page loads with a single pane.
8. Resize the window below 768px. Expect: only the active pane visible; back button navigates pane history.
9. Set OS to reduced-motion. Expect: no opacity/scroll transitions.
10. Lighthouse a11y on a stacked URL. Expect score ≥ today's baseline.
11. `pnpm --filter @pattern-plgrnd/patterns build`. Expect: build succeeds; static output for every `/patterns/<slug>` page unchanged.

### Out of scope

- Persisting stack history across sessions (URL is the source of truth).
- Visual "spine" rotation on sticky pinned panes — ship as a follow-up if the basic stack feels solid.
- Stack-aware preloading of likely next panes — premature; cache on click is enough.
- Cross-pane search / linking back to the same slug already in the stack — Andy lets duplicates exist; we will too.
